  "conclusions": [
    "A +/-10% global mu_nu_mu stress changes the total B.1 source by only about +/-0.21%.",
    "A +/-30% global mu_nu_mu stress changes the total B.1 source by +0.555%/-0.656%; setting mu_nu_mu=0 changes it by +1.174%.",
    "Even setting mu_nu_mu=0 only reduces the weak-end source deficit from 9.03% to 7.96%.",
    "The 8--15 km shell-only +/-30% stress changes the total source by +0.158%/-0.211%; setting mu_nu_mu=0 only in that shell changes it by +0.313%.",
    "The paper's mu_nu_tau=0 assumption is also not a large source lever in this reconstructed profile: the extreme diagnostic mu_nu_tau=mu_nu_mu changes B.1 by -1.174%; the sign of mu_nu_tau is irrelevant for the pair kernel.",
    "The local neutrino-pair kernel is even in each chemical potential, so a global sign flip of mu_nu_mu gives exactly the baseline source.",
    "These are source-only stress tests, not inferred profile uncertainties; B.2 is not recomputed here."
